Full-core Pyrope and external RTL comparison
=============================================

The 2026-09-19 regeneration uses CVA6 commit
6cb200105fb9441d170e45786125a737fab98e91, configuration
cv64a6_imafdc_sv39_wb. generation/provenance.json records the CVFPU revision;
generation/source.patch and generation/cvfpu.patch capture the existing
Slang-compatible source rewrites used for generation. Apply those patches to
the matching external checkout (the second patch inside core/cvfpu).
The suite's verilog/ directory contains only the tag_cmp cone, not this core.

Generate with a LiveHD build containing the September 19 simulation/translation
repairs:

  export CVA6_REPO_DIR=/absolute/path/to/cva6
  export HPDCACHE_DIR=$CVA6_REPO_DIR/core/cache_subsystem/hpdcache
  export TARGET_CFG=cv64a6_imafdc_sv39_wb
  lhd compile --top cva6 --emit-dir pyrope:tmp_cva6 --workdir tmp_generate -- \
    --allow-use-before-declare -DSYNTHESIS \
    --translate-off-format=pragma,translate_off,translate_on \
    "$CVA6_REPO_DIR/core/include/${TARGET_CFG}_config_pkg.sv" \
    -F "$CVA6_REPO_DIR/core/Flist.cva6"

Refresh tag_cmp_wrap separately from verilog/filelist.f (NR_PORTS=5), retaining
the full core's tag_cmp implementation. Refresh tests/comment1 and tests/bug1
against the new tag_cmp; the bug ignores way zero's valid bit.

Run the independent whole-core Verilator twin, both LHD input paths, and a
one-module semantic incremental edit against a cache-disabled oracle:

  python3 cva6/check_sim.py --lhd /absolute/path/to/lhd \
    --rtl "$CVA6_REPO_DIR" --suite . --work /tmp/cva6-comparison

Use a new --work directory. Requires Verilator, make, and a C++ compiler.
The runner emits a fresh Pyrope tree from the same RTL inputs used by the
Verilog simulation leg, following the source-generation command above. It uses that output directly, without copying the
checked-in Pyrope or applying post-generation fixes. Translation failures must
be fixed in the Slang frontend/Pyrope writer and covered by a reduced positive
round-trip regression; simulator failures belong in the simulator.

The runner records commands, wall times, LHD phase reports and the binary hash
in statistics.json. Setup, host compilation, and three execution samples are
separate; tuning and VCD are disabled. It mutates only the generated scratch tree.
The existing architectural assertions stay enabled.

At 50,000 cycles all three paths produce x2=100, x3=-100, marker=1445,
43,443 retirements, zero exceptions, and completion at cycle 738. This is
program simulation evidence, not a whole-core formal equivalence proof.
Focused RTL-to-Pyrope regressions and individual core modules prove with CVC5;
whole-core LEC remains limited by unsupported FPU proof structure/timeouts.
